  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Inferring from the tense",
     "texto": [
      "**듯하다** presents an inference: with adjectives in the present, **-(으)ㄴ 듯하다** is used (피곤한 듯해요 = seems tired); with verbs in the present, **-는 듯하다** (쉬는 듯해요 = seems to be resting); with verbs for the future, **-(으)ㄹ 듯하다** (올 듯해요 = seems it will come). With nouns: 학생인 듯해요 = seems to be a student."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Nuance and register",
     "texto": [
      "**-(으)ㄴ/는 듯하다** appears a lot in explanations and careful texts; **-나 보다** is common in conversational inferences, while **-(으)ㄹ 것 같다** serves for many opinions and predictions. They are not exact equivalents of «more certain» or «softer»: the nuance depends on the context."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
